# A forged packet number: a later packet taken for a lost one before it. It was a known limit (owner, 2026-11-17). With the data masked from the header CRC, a header that noise has forged takes the wrong mask off its data, and the data checksum fails
# found by linksearch --rules hl-mask
sizes number_bits=3 max_words=1 window=2 zeros=40 flush_zeros=32 status_timer=24 queue=8 reask=96 pass=1 restart_words=1 delay=1 words=1 images=0 window0=0 wrong=0 still=0
packets 2 0 0 0
offer 0 1 216
fate 0 5 gone
offer 0 1 233
fate 0 6 forge-number-back
quiet 271 20000
run hl-mask fail word 1 delivered where word 0 was next
run hl ok
